== Viva / Card Questions

=== Urology
- *Hematuria:* Definition, types. Painless vs. painful causes (transitional cell ca vs. stones/infection). Microscopic hematuria causes (drug-induced/antiplatelets). Triple tumors. Investigations. 
- *Prostate & Bladder:* BPH vs. Prostate Ca (DRE findings, PSA values, TRUS biopsy). Bladder Ca (TURBT procedure, grading, staging, chemo/radio). 
- *Testis/Scrotum:* Testicular torsion (D/D, Phren's sign, management within 6 hrs, why operate on the other testis, testicular prosthesis). Hydrocele, pyocele, hematocele. 
- *Kidney:* RCC (presentation, treatment). Renal vs. Pulmonary TB (diagnosis, gold standard tests, treatment duration). Types of kidney stones. 
- *Urethra/Catheter:* Urethral rupture (triad, urethroplasty timing). Catheterization steps (counseling, assurance, lubrication). Circumcision (methods, end arteries, paraphimosis).

=== Orthopedics
- *Fractures & Complications:* Classification. Healing process of long bones. Upper vs. lower limb plaster cast durations. Immediate vs. delayed complications. Fat embolism. Compartment syndrome. Volkmann's ischemic contracture. Delayed union, non-union, mal-union. 
- *Specific Fractures:* Supracondylar fracture (nerve/artery injuries, immediate cast). Colles fracture (mechanism, cast position). Femur fracture (Shenton's line, fixation types, weight-bearing). 
- *Infections & Tumors:* Acute vs. Chronic Osteomyelitis (organisms, features, timeline for empirical antibiotics, X-ray findings, sequestrum, involucrum). Benign vs. malignant bone tumors (epiphysis vs. metaphysis vs. diaphysis, sarcoma metastasis routes). 

=== General Surgery, Trauma & Burns
- *Hemorrhage & Shock:* Primary, reactionary, secondary hemorrhage definitions and management. Massive blood transfusion (complications, mismatch reactions, graft vs. host). Types of shock, differentiating septic from hemorrhagic shock. 
- *Burns:* Inhalational vs. electrical burns (arrhythmia risks). Rule of 2 / Rule of 9. Fluid calculation and distribution (first 8 hrs vs. next 16 hrs, what if the patient arrives late?). Deep vs. superficial burn presentation. Hospitalization indications. 
- *Trauma/Head Injury:* Blunt abdominal trauma. Extradural vs. subdural hematoma. Lucid interval. GCS scoring. Raised ICP signs (Cushing's triad). Hospitalization indications for head injury.
- *Wounds & Infections:* Tetanus-prone wounds, toxoid protocol (Bailey & Love). Wound infection management (Eusol, Vinegar for pseudomonas). Cut wrist management (tourniquet use, primary vs. delayed closure). Carbuncle definition and organisms. Sinus vs. Fistula (Goodsall's rule, high vs. low). 

=== Anesthesia, Fluids & Misc.
- *Anesthesia:* GA stages, triad, amnesia. Neuromuscular blockers. LA drugs (blue vs. red bottles—Lidocaine vs. Adrenaline). Why use adrenaline, where is it contraindicated (end arteries). Spinal anesthesia.
- *Fluids:* Post-op fluid calculation (2.5L breakdown). Hartmann's vs. Normal Saline vs. Ringer's Lactate (K+ concentration, preventing acidosis). Urine output targets. 
- *Misc Topics:* Buerger's disease (intermittent claudication, resting pain, ABPI, amputation levels). Pneumothorax vs. Hemothorax (Triangle of safety, ICT indications and removal, water seal check). Autoclave principles (121°C). Cystic hygroma (brilliantly transilluminant). Intussusception vs. Hirschsprung disease in pediatrics.